{"step_index":2175,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:47:08Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:17:08+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:17:08+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/README.md`\nTotal Lines: 131\nTotal Bytes: 4138\nShowing lines 1 to 131\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🛡️ SmartAGENT\n2: \n3: **Autonomous AI Cybersecurity Agent** — powered by [Fluxnat Coder 3B](https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B).\n4: \n5: An agentic security AI that can autonomously scan codebases, find vulnerabilities, trace data flows, and generate fixes — all running locally on your GPU.\n6: \n7: ---\n8: \n9: ## 🌟 Highlights\n10: \n11: - **🤖 Agentic Mode:** ReAct reasoning loop (Thought → Action → Observation) with 8 security tools and interactive CLI chat.\n12: - **🧠 Fluxnat Coder 3B:** Custom fine-tuned 3B cybersecurity SLM. Uncensored. No safety filters. Built by Fluxnat.\n13: - **⚡ Hybrid Scanning:** 4 deterministic SAST scanners + AI Chain-of-Thought reasoning + security scoring (A+ to F).\n14: - **🔧 60+ Terminal Commands:** The agent can run git, curl, nmap, docker, semgrep, and more — sandboxed.\n15: - **💻 Runs Locally:** 4-bit quantization fits on a GTX 1650 (4GB VRAM). No cloud API needed.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## 🚀 Quick Start\n20: \n21: ```bash\n22: # Install\n23: pip install -e .\n24: \n25: # Interactive agent chat\n26: smartagent chat\n27: \n28: # One-shot autonomous task\n29: smartagent agent \"scan this project for SQL injection and suggest fixes\"\n30: \n31: # Classic static scan\n32: smartagent scan .\n33: \n34: # AI-verified scan (uses Fluxnat Coder 3B)\n35: smartagent scan . --ai\n36: \n37: # Export reports\n38: smartagent scan . --json report.json --md report.md\n39: \n40: # System info\n41: smartagent info\n42: ```\n43: \n44: ---\n45: \n46: ## 🤖 Agentic Mode\n47: \n48: Chat with SmartAGENT like a real security engineer:\n49: \n50: ```\n<truncated 1124 bytes>\nject Structure\n84: \n85: ```\n86: smartAGENT/\n87: ├── smartagent/\n88: │   ├── cli.py                  # CLI (chat, agent, scan, train, info)\n89: │   ├── config.py               # Configuration\n90: │   ├── agent/                  # ReAct Agent\n91: │   │   ├── core.py             # Reasoning loop\n92: │   │   ├── tools.py            # 8 security tools + CWE database\n93: │   │   ├── memory.py           # Conversation memory\n94: │   │   └── prompts.py          # System prompts\n95: │   ├── scanners/               # Static Analysis\n96: │   │   ├── pattern_scanner.py  # SQLi, RCE, XSS, Deserialization\n97: │   │   ├── secret_scanner.py   # API keys, tokens, credentials\n98: │   │   ├── dependency_scanner.py # CVE lookups via OSV.dev\n99: │   │   └── config_scanner.py   # Dockerfile & .env misconfigs\n100: │   ├── ai/                     # LLM Engine\n101: │   │   ├── model.py            # Model loader & streaming\n102: │   │   ├── judge.py            # AI verification & fix generation\n103: │   │   └── prompts.py          # CoT prompt templates\n104: │   └── reporting/              # Output\n105: │       ├── report.py           # Rich terminal UI & exports\n106: │       └── scorer.py           # Security grading (A+ to F)\n107: ├── pyproject.toml\n108: └── tests/\n109: ```\n110: \n111: ---\n112: \n113: ## 🔧 Training (Optional)\n114: \n115: If you want to retrain or fine-tune the model yourself:\n116: \n117: **Google Colab (Free T4 GPU):** Upload `Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb` → Run all cells.\n118: \n119: **Local:**\n120: ```bash\n121: python prepare_datasets.py\n122: python train.py\n123: python merge_and_export.py\n124: ```\n125: \n126: ---\n127: \n128: ## ⚖️ License\n129: \n130: Apache-2.0 — Built for defensive security auditing and authorized penetration testing.\n131: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
