{"step_index":2183,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-16T07:47:44Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-16T13:17:44+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-16T13:17:47+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/docs/model.md`\nTotal Lines: 154\nTotal Bytes: 4690\nShowing lines 1 to 154\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # Fluxnat Coder 3B — Model Documentation\n2: \n3: **[🤗 Hugging Face → k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B](https://huggingface.co/k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B)**\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## What Is It\n8: \n9: Fluxnat Coder 3B is a **3-billion parameter cybersecurity AI** built by Fluxnat. It performs autonomous source code vulnerability auditing — finding security flaws, explaining root causes, mapping to CWE/OWASP standards, and generating production-ready fixes.\n10: \n11: **Key traits:**\n12: - 🔓 **Uncensored** — No safety refusals. Will analyze any code, any vulnerability, any exploit pattern.\n13: - ⚡ **Lightweight** — Runs on a GTX 1650 (4GB VRAM) in 4-bit quantization.\n14: - 🧠 **Chain-of-Thought** — Explains *why* code is vulnerable, not just *that* it is.\n15: - 🎯 **Security-Specialized** — Purpose-built for vulnerability detection, not general chat.\n16: \n17: ---\n18: \n19: ## What It Can Do\n20: \n21: ### Vulnerability Detection\n22: - SQL Injection (CWE-89)\n23: - OS Command Injection (CWE-78)\n24: - Path Traversal (CWE-22)\n25: - Cross-Site Scripting / XSS (CWE-79)\n26: - Insecure Deserialization (CWE-502)\n27: - Server-Side Request Forgery / SSRF (CWE-918)\n28: - Buffer Overflow (CWE-122)\n29: - Hardcoded Credentials (CWE-798)\n30: - Eval/Exec Injection (CWE-95)\n31: - Weak Cryptography (CWE-327/328)\n32: \n33: ### Supported Languages\n34: \n35: | Language | Vulnerability Coverage |\n36: |---|---|\n37: | **Python** | SQLi, Command Injection, Path Traversal, Pickle/YAML Deserialization, SSRF, Secrets |\n38: | **JavaScript / Node.js** | DOM XSS, `child_process.exec`, Protot\n<truncated 1795 bytes>\nnt\": \"\"\"Audit this code for vulnerabilities:\n85: \n86: @app.route('/lookup')\n87: def lookup():\n88:     user = request.args.get('user')\n89:     query = f\"SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '{user}'\"\n90:     return db.execute(query).fetchall()\n91: \"\"\"},\n92: ]\n93: \n94: text = tokenizer.apply_chat_template(messages, tokenize=False, add_generation_prompt=True)\n95: inputs = tokenizer(text, return_tensors=\"pt\").to(model.device)\n96: \n97: outputs = model.generate(**inputs, max_new_tokens=512, temperature=0.2, top_p=0.95)\n98: response = tokenizer.decode(outputs[0][inputs.input_ids.shape[1]:], skip_special_tokens=True)\n99: print(response)\n100: ```\n101: \n102: ### 4-Bit Quantized (Low VRAM)\n103: \n104: ```python\n105: from transformers import BitsAndBytesConfig\n106: \n107: bnb_config = BitsAndBytesConfig(\n108:     load_in_4bit=True,\n109:     bnb_4bit_quant_type=\"nf4\",\n110:     bnb_4bit_compute_dtype=torch.float16,\n111: )\n112: \n113: model = AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained(\n114:     \"k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B\",\n115:     quantization_config=bnb_config,\n116:     device_map=\"auto\",\n117:     trust_remote_code=True,\n118: )\n119: ```\n120: \n121: ### vLLM (Production API Server)\n122: \n123: ```bash\n124: python -m vllm.entrypoints.openai.api_server \\\n125:     --model k4ran909/Fluxnat-Coder-3B \\\n126:     --dtype float16 \\\n127:     --max-model-len 4096 \\\n128:     --port 8000\n129: ```\n130: \n131: ### SmartAGENT CLI (Easiest)\n132: \n133: ```bash\n134: pip install -e .\n135: smartagent chat          # Interactive agent\n136: smartagent scan . --ai   # AI-verified scan\n137: ```\n138: \n139: ---\n140: \n141: ## Hardware Requirements\n142: \n143: | Mode | VRAM | GPU Examples |\n144: |---|---|---|\n145: | 4-bit quantized | ~1.8 GB | GTX 1650, RTX 2060, T4 |\n146: | 16-bit (float16) | ~6 GB | RTX 3060, RTX 4060, A10 |\n147: | CPU only | 8+ GB RAM | Any modern CPU (slow) |\n148: \n149: ---\n150: \n151: ## License\n152: \n153: Apache-2.0 — Free for commercial and non-commercial use.\n154: \nThe above content shows the entire, complete file contents of the requested file.\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
